          "content": {
            "size": 6126,
            "mimeType": "text/css; charset=utf-8",
            "compression": 3072,
            "text": "/* The menu at the top of every bapas-diary.com page, shared so it sits in exactly the same place on each one\n   (Darpan, 24 Oct 2026: \"keep them in position, but just fade them out gently\"). Use it as\n     <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/menu.css\">\n     <nav class=\"site-menu\" aria-label=\"Website tabs\"><a href=\"/\">Today</a><a href=\"/calendar/\">Calendar</a>\n       <a href=\"/search/\">Search</a><a href=\"/travels/\">Travels</a><a href=\"/through-the-years/\">Through the years</a>\n       <a href=\"/about/\">About</a></nav>\n   (the deploy puts the tabs in this order on every page anyway: tools/site_menu.py)\n   with class=\"on\" aria-current=\"page\" on the page's own tab, as the very first thing in <body>, and 46px of\n   room left at the top of the page under it. It scrolls away with the page; add class \"stay\" to keep it pinned (pages that do not scroll, like Travels). */\n.site-menu {\n  box-sizing: border-box; position: absolute; top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px); left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 50; height: 46px;\n  display: flex; justify-content: safe center; align-items: flex-end; flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 0 clamp(12px, 3vw, 26px);\n  padding: 0 max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px)) 6px max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px));\n  overflow-x: auto; scrollbar-width: none;\n  view-transition-name: site-menu;   /* stays still while the page under it fades */\n}\n/* pinned, with a soft dark fade behind it so it stays readable over the page */\n.site-menu.stay { position: fixed; background: linear-gradient(rgba(10, 8, 20, .85), rgba(10, 8, 20, 0)); }\n.site-menu::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }\n.site-menu a {\n  box-sizing: border-box; flex: none; font: 700 11px/1 Arimo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing: .26em; text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: #d9a441; text-decoration: none; padding: 6px 0 5px; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent; white-space: nowrap;\n}\n.site-menu a:hover, .site-menu a.on { color: #ffe296; border-bottom-color: #d9a441; }\n/* scroll bars in the site's gold instead of the bright grey ones Windows draws by default */\nhtml { scrollbar-color: rgba(217, 164, 65, .55) transparent; }\n@media (max-width: 600px) { .site-menu { gap: 0 10px; } .site-menu a { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; } }   /* on the narrowest phones the row can be swiped */\n.site-menu a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #ffe296; outline-offset: 3px; }\n/* moving between pages: a gentle fade (browsers without this simply switch pages) */\n@view-transition { navigation: auto; }\n::view-transition-old(root), ::view-transition-new(root) { animation-duration: .45s; animation-timing-function: ease; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { ::view-transition-old(root), ::view-transition-new(root) { animation: none; } }\n/* Darpan, 25 Oct 2026: no dark edge round the page, text size and language buttons in the top right corner on computers,\n   the page you are on clearly lit up, a little more room between the tabs. nav.site-menu (not .site-menu) so a page's own\n   class of the same name (the Calendar's travel stops are also called .stay) can't change the menu */\nhtml, body { margin: 0; }\nnav.site-menu { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 0 clamp(18px, 3.2vw, 36px); border: 0; border-radius: 0; opacity: 1; transform: none;\n  font-size: inherit; line-height: normal; cursor: auto; color: inherit;\n  padding: 0 max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px)) 6px max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px)); }\nnav.site-menu a.on { color: #fff3cf; background: rgba(255, 211, 107, .16); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 211, 107, .65); border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 6px 13px 5px; text-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(255, 211, 107, .55); }\n@media (max-width: 600px) { nav.site-menu { gap: 0 10px; } }\n@media (min-width: 761px) {\n  nav.site-menu { padding-right: 236px; }\n  nav.site-menu .bd-aa, nav.site-menu .gu-switch { position: absolute; top: 10px; margin: 0; }\n  nav.site-menu .gu-switch { right: 16px; }\n  nav.site-menu .bd-aa { right: 124px; }\n}\n@media (min-width: 761px) and (max-width: 1199px) { nav.site-menu { gap: 0 14px; } nav.site-menu a { letter-spacing: .14em; } }\n@media (min-width: 1200px) { nav.site-menu { padding-left: 236px; } }   /* same room both sides, so the tabs stay in the middle */\n/* Tablets (761 to 1199px), Darpan, 28 Oct 2026: on his mum's tablet the tabs sat to the left of the middle, because all the\n   buttons took room on the right only. There is not enough width for the same room both sides with all of them on the\n   right, so on tablets Aa moves to the top left corner (with Save for travelling on iPads, site/offline/offline.css) and\n   the language switch stays top right: the same room each side, the tabs in the middle of the screen */\n@media (min-width: 761px) and (max-width: 1199px) {\n  nav.site-menu { padding-left: 128px; padding-right: 128px; }\n  nav.site-menu .bd-aa { right: auto; left: 16px; }\n}\n/* Darpan, 26 Oct 2026: \"these always stay at the top of the screen. If someone scrolls down, they just go very faint, but\n   still keep them there so you can click on it whenever you want to.\" Computers and tablets only: phones keep the tab bar\n   at the bottom. tools/site_menu.py adds the few lines that switch on .faint once the page has moved 40px. */\n@media (min-width: 761px) {\n  nav.site-menu, nav.site-menu.stay { position: fixed; background: linear-gradient(rgba(34, 12, 16, .92), rgba(34, 12, 16, .78));\n    backdrop-filter: blur(6px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(6px); transition: opacity .6s ease; }\n  nav.site-menu.faint { opacity: .28; }\n  nav.site-menu.faint:hover, nav.site-menu.faint:focus-within { opacity: 1; transition-duration: .25s; }\n}\n/* iPads held upright (761 to 959px) with seven tabs: a little tighter, and \"Through the years\" says \"Years\" as on phones,\n   so every tab fits beside the Aa and language buttons (Then and now tab, 26 Oct 2026) */\n@media (min-width: 761px) and (max-width: 959px) {\n  nav.site-menu { gap: 0 12px; }\n  nav.site-menu a { letter-spacing: .08em; }\n  nav.site-menu a[href=\"/through-the-years/\"] { font-size: 0; }\n  nav.site-menu a[href=\"/through-the-years/\"]::after { content: \"Years\"; font-size: 11px; }\n}\n"
